The node is granted only `aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0`, and the `with` clause is its entire authority. I left out the two operations requests: writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs a filesystem capability, and calling the metadata service needs an HTTP capability, and this world has neither. Adding either would widen the node's authority beyond its grant. Those requests need to go to whoever owns the graph's capability grants.

I also chose to record considered ids only when `published` is true, since unpublished items were never shown to anyone. If the graph intends to mark every considered item seen regardless, remove the `if published.published` guard.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{published-digest, run-report};

    import aap:caps/state-rw@0.1.0;

    export run: func(published: published-digest) -> run-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_rw;

struct Node;

const SEEN_PREFIX: &str = "seen:";

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(published: PublishedDigest) -> RunReport {
        // Mark every considered item as seen, but only if the digest was
        // actually published: unpublished items were never shown to anyone.
        let mut recorded: u32 = 0;
        if published.published {
            for id in published.considered.iter() {
                if id.is_empty() {
                    continue;
                }
                let key = format!("{}{}", SEEN_PREFIX, id);
                state_rw::put(&key, "1");
                recorded = recorded.saturating_add(1);
            }
        }

        RunReport {
            date: published.date,
            recorded,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

